# Technical document line breaks

When editing **technical** Markdown in this repo (`docs/`, `notes/`, result indexes, README/AGENTS):

- Put **one sentence per line** (semantic line breaks).
- Do **not** hard-wrap mid-sentence to a column width (e.g. do not end a line with `in` and start the next with `Documents.`).
- A new line may start a new sentence, a list item, a heading, or a blank line between blocks.
- Keep Markdown links and pathnames on one line when they belong to one sentence, even if the line is long.

When writing **ordinary prose** (email drafts, narrative notes the user asked for as flowing paragraphs, chat replies that are not project docs): use normal paragraphs; this rule does not apply.

## Example

Bad (wrap mid-sentence):

```markdown
macOS may block automatic runs from reading a project on your Desktop or in
Documents. Give Python Full Disk Access.
```

Good (sentence boundaries):

```markdown
macOS may block automatic runs from reading a project on your Desktop or in Documents.
Give Python Full Disk Access.
```
